<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions (W2-C gate, P2-16).

  The gate (pom.xml) fails the build on CVSS >= 7 (failBuildOnCVSS=7).
  This file is the DOCUMENTED registry of known findings: every entry
  carries the CVE, the affected dependency, the fix version, the owner
  and the expiry condition. Deleting an entry is the acceptance proof
  when the owning lane bumps the dependency; an entry without a reason
  and an owner must not be added.

  ACTIVE FINDINGS: none.

  The two entries this file once carried (W2-C, measured 2026-09-22 against
  branch feature/frontend HEAD, plugin 12.1.9) were both CVSS v3.1 base 5.3
  (MEDIUM — below the CVSS 7 gate threshold) and both owned by W3-C:
    - commons-lang3 3.17.0 / CVE-2025-48924 (uncontrolled recursion) —
      W3-C bumped commons-lang3 to 3.19.0 (fix landed at 3.18.0); entry
      deleted.
    - jackson-databind 2.21.4 / CVE-2026-54515 (case-insensitive-binding
      deserializer leak) — W3-C bumped jackson-bom to 2.21.7 (fix landed at
      2.21.5); entry deleted.
  W3-C also bumped tomcat 10.1.55 -> 10.1.60 and bcprov 1.78.1 -> 1.86 on
  the same pass (advisory-driven, not tracked here because neither was a
  suppressed below-threshold finding — they sat inside the managed Boot line
  and the explicit BC pin respectively). Re-add an entry below (CVE,
  dependency, fix version, owner, expiry) whenever a future scan surfaces a
  below-threshold finding you are deliberately not fixing yet.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression/1.3.0"
              xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
              xsi:schemaLocation="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression/1.3.0 https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/css/dependency-suppression-1.3.0.xsd">
</suppressions>
